== B6 (R-C): half-rung consistency ==
  per-half-step amplitude sqrt(1-eps) = 0.983987481401:
  a multiplicative law D(x) = (1-eps)^x is the ONLY form in the
  route list that is exact at x = 1/2 with a single per-half-step
  amplitude (Born reading: rung index counts amplitude powers);
  additive or quadratic laws have no consistent half-step.  This
  is a CONSISTENCY argument favoring the product/leakage class,
  not a derivation, and is graded as such.

